WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.701 --> 00:00:02.067
-Henrik...

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.868
You're wearing your --
-Oh, oh.

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:05.234
-Yeah, sorry.
You're wearing your --

00:00:05.234 --> 00:00:07.901
You're wearing your goalie mask,
yeah, on Friday the 13th.

00:00:07.901 --> 00:00:10.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
Much better. Much better.

00:00:10.167 --> 00:00:12.834
Oh, my gosh.
Happy Friday the 13th.

00:00:12.834 --> 00:00:15.067
-Happy 13th.
-Thank you for --

00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:17.367
thanks for being here
and coming back to the show.

00:00:17.367 --> 00:00:19.167
We always love having you on.
-Thanks for having me.

00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:21.133
-The last time you were
on our show

00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:24.334
was right before you were --
they were retiring your jersey.

00:00:24.334 --> 00:00:26.234
-Yes.
-In the Garden.

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:28.234
And it was unbelievable.

00:00:28.234 --> 00:00:30.901
I think I have
a photo of it here.

00:00:30.901 --> 00:00:33.601
This is it right here.
Number 30 right there.

00:00:33.601 --> 00:00:35.701
-Yeah.
It was just incredible.

00:00:35.701 --> 00:00:37.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:37.601 --> 00:00:40.767
You know, to have an opportunity
to bring in your family,

00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:43.067
closest friends,
and share that moment

00:00:43.067 --> 00:00:44.601
is something
I'll never forget.

00:00:44.601 --> 00:00:46.267
-Yeah.
-It was the first time my family

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:48.400
was together in New York.
For different reasons --

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.434
My brother's always played
throughout my career,

00:00:50.434 --> 00:00:52.234
so he didn't have
the opportunity to come here.

00:00:52.234 --> 00:00:56.300
So, obviously, to share
that moment, and, you know...

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:57.901
-Well, the city loves you
so much.

00:00:57.901 --> 00:00:59.634
-I appreciate it.
-And I love seeing --

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:02.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
We do.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:07.100
The greatest.
The last time I saw you,

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.067
I don't know
if you remember this.

00:01:09.067 --> 00:01:11.834
We sat next to each other
at a Harry Styles concert.

00:01:11.834 --> 00:01:14.033
-That's right.
[ Cheering ]

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:16.367
It was boa night at the Garden.

00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:18.267
-Here's a selfie that we took.

00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:21.467
This is -- you were wearing --
Yeah, you were wearing a boa.

00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:23.601
-There it is.
-I want to s--

00:01:23.601 --> 00:01:25.901
Well, I want to say,
I think that

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:28.801
you kind of owe me a little bit
because I'll tell you what.

00:01:28.801 --> 00:01:31.067
I took a little heat
because I was --

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:33.400
I was dad dancing at Harry --
'Cause I didn't know

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.434
how to dance
at a Harry Styles concert.

00:01:35.434 --> 00:01:38.334
And you were --
you were there right next to me.

00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:40.267
And all these videos
are going around of me

00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:41.801
just kind of not knowing
how to dance.

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.601
[ Laughter ]
But you were right behind me.

00:01:43.601 --> 00:01:45.300
I'm like, "That's Lundqvist.
That's --

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.000
That's Henrik Lundqvist
right behind me,

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.868
with a boa, going crazy."

00:01:48.868 --> 00:01:51.167
You were like, "Yeah!",
screaming.

00:01:51.167 --> 00:01:52.467
You love Harry Styles.

00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:53.968
-I was just
following your lead that night.

00:01:53.968 --> 00:01:56.267
But it was, uh...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:57.801
You know what?

00:01:57.801 --> 00:02:01.267
I have this great opportunity.
I work a lot at the Garden now.

00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:03.601
Not playing hockey,
but I may see people.

00:02:03.601 --> 00:02:05.267
I go to these amazing concerts.

00:02:05.267 --> 00:02:07.834
And Harry --
that was incredible show.

00:02:07.834 --> 00:02:09.167
-Wasn't that unbelievable?
-It was.

00:02:09.167 --> 00:02:10.667
I brought my kids
for one show,

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:12.501
and I just looked at them.

00:02:12.501 --> 00:02:14.634
It felt like we were watching
Elvis or something.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.534
Everybody was just screaming.
I was clapping my hands.

00:02:16.534 --> 00:02:17.734
My daughter looked at me,
she's like,

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:20.133
"Dad, we're not clapping.
We're screaming."

00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:21.734
-Yeah, yeah,
yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:21.734 --> 00:02:23.434
"Dad, just stop.
Just don't do anything.

00:02:23.434 --> 00:02:24.801
Just sit down."
-"Don't embarrass me."

00:02:24.801 --> 00:02:27.501
-Exactly.
That's exactly right.

00:02:27.501 --> 00:02:30.634
Now you're about to be inducted
into the Hockey Hall of Fame.

00:02:30.634 --> 00:02:31.968
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:31.968 --> 00:02:35.033
-Buddy, congratulations.
I'm so --

00:02:35.033 --> 00:02:38.801
You know, I'm honored
to know you, but, I mean,

00:02:38.801 --> 00:02:40.868
it must mean a lot to you.
As a kid growing up,

00:02:40.868 --> 00:02:42.133
you go,
"Well, I just want to --"

00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:44.100
You'd be lucky to play
in the league,

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:45.467
let alone be
in the Hall of Fame.

00:02:45.467 --> 00:02:47.400
-Listen, it's not something
you really

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.234
dream about growing up.

00:02:49.234 --> 00:02:51.667
Because what you're dreaming
about is to make the league,

00:02:51.667 --> 00:02:55.067
play in the NHL,
and get that opportunity.

00:02:55.067 --> 00:02:57.033
You don't really think about
how it's going to end, right?

00:02:57.033 --> 00:02:58.400
But here we are,

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:02.567
and I'm just so grateful
and honored to be included.

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:04.934
A lot of those players
that are in the Hall of Fame,

00:03:04.934 --> 00:03:08.033
for me, they were idols,
people that I looked up to,

00:03:08.033 --> 00:03:11.067
and it's just going to be
a great moment

00:03:11.067 --> 00:03:12.467
for me and my family.

00:03:12.467 --> 00:03:15.567
And, you know, I thought about
this backstage.

00:03:15.567 --> 00:03:17.601
Last time, yeah,
my jersey went up.

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:19.734
-Yeah.
-Now Hall of Fame.

00:03:19.734 --> 00:03:21.067
I'm just excited.
Next time I come here,

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:22.667
I don't know if I just landed
on the Moon or something.

00:03:22.667 --> 00:03:23.934
-You're gonna land --
Yeah, you're gonna have to

00:03:23.934 --> 00:03:25.701
have to go to the --
Every time you come on the show,

00:03:25.701 --> 00:03:27.400
it's another giant thing.
-Unbelievable.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:29.534
-Exactly.
Every single time.

00:03:29.534 --> 00:03:30.968
Let's get.
-Thank you. Thank you for that.

00:03:30.968 --> 00:03:34.033
-Let's get Henrik to space.
I can call somebody.

00:03:34.033 --> 00:03:37.200
We'll make a good...
But I do want to talk about this

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.234
next chapter
that you're doing right now,

00:03:39.234 --> 00:03:40.734
because this is --
you're coming out --

00:03:40.734 --> 00:03:42.000
You have your own fragrance.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.667
-Yes. We just launched
this, Next Chapter.

00:03:44.667 --> 00:03:47.801
-You're stylish,
so I trust you on this stuff.

00:03:47.801 --> 00:03:50.234
But how much work goes into this
when you're doing it.

00:03:50.234 --> 00:03:52.968
-A lot, actually.
This is a niche fragrance,

00:03:52.968 --> 00:03:55.133
which means it takes
a lot longer.

00:03:55.133 --> 00:03:58.734
Think about it like wine,
for example.

00:03:58.734 --> 00:04:00.734
Really nice wine
takes a long time.

00:04:00.734 --> 00:04:04.634
This took about 12 to 14 months
to develop.

00:04:04.634 --> 00:04:07.868
Regular fragrance of perfume
takes about a week, two weeks.

00:04:07.868 --> 00:04:11.000
But when it's a niche perfume
or fragrance, months.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.133
-Really?
And do you do a lot of smelling

00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:15.267
and sniff tests?
-Oh, yeah, a lot.

00:04:15.267 --> 00:04:17.000
-I think after like
three different smells --

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.200
'Cause I do that with candles.

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:20.133
I go, "I'm good.
Everything smells the same."

00:04:20.133 --> 00:04:22.033
-Well,
the trick is coffee beans.

00:04:22.033 --> 00:04:24.667
Coffee beans
in between to reset.

00:04:24.667 --> 00:04:26.100
That's what I learned.
-It's like a palate cleanser.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:27.801
-Yes, yes.
-A coffee bean.

00:04:27.801 --> 00:04:29.167
All right.
So you have two here.

00:04:29.167 --> 00:04:30.767
What is this?
Volume one and volume two.

00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:32.534
-Yes.
-Of Next Chapter.

00:04:32.534 --> 00:04:34.801
Now, which one do you think
is best for me?

00:04:34.801 --> 00:04:36.501
-We'll try this.
A little more nighttime.

00:04:36.501 --> 00:04:37.801
You're in a suit.
-Yeah.

00:04:37.801 --> 00:04:39.467
-Yeah. Why not?

00:04:39.467 --> 00:04:41.534
-Now, here's the way I do it.
I spray it.

00:04:41.534 --> 00:04:43.133
-Oh, you spray...
-And then I go.

00:04:43.133 --> 00:04:45.033
-Oh, you do the walk-in,
the walk-in.

00:04:45.033 --> 00:04:46.300
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:47.567
-Ooh!
-Oh.

00:04:47.567 --> 00:04:48.901
-I love this.
-Oh, you love it?

00:04:48.901 --> 00:04:51.000
-I feel like a new man.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:53.000
This is studly.
This is --

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.801
I love this.
-That's good.

00:04:54.801 --> 00:04:57.067
-I don't know how to describe.
What -- What --

00:04:57.067 --> 00:04:59.834
-Can you tell the notes?

00:04:59.834 --> 00:05:01.167
-I just played a game with
Kelly.

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:03.734
I really have done all I can.

00:05:03.734 --> 00:05:05.634
I --
It smells great, though.

00:05:05.634 --> 00:05:08.267
I know that.
I really love -- it's fresh.

00:05:08.267 --> 00:05:11.033
It is kind of
a nighttimey type of vibe.

00:05:11.033 --> 00:05:14.234
Is there, like, a --
I'm gonna get really nerdy here.

00:05:14.234 --> 00:05:18.033
Is there a vetiver
type of a scent?

00:05:18.033 --> 00:05:19.834
Did I make that up?
No, no?

00:05:19.834 --> 00:05:21.334
-You have that, a little pepper.

00:05:21.334 --> 00:05:22.667
-A little pepper in there?
-Ginger.

00:05:22.667 --> 00:05:23.934
-Yeah.
-Little ginger.

00:05:23.934 --> 00:05:25.167
Can you --
Can you sense that?

00:05:25.167 --> 00:05:26.701
-This is wild.
Now let me try the other one.

00:05:26.701 --> 00:05:28.634
Can you spray the other one?
I won't dive into this --

00:05:28.634 --> 00:05:30.200
Well, why not?
I'll dive in.

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:32.133
Let me dive into this.
This is Volume One

00:05:32.133 --> 00:05:34.434
of Next Chapter.
Yeah.

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:35.834
-Oh, there we go.
-Ooh.

00:05:35.834 --> 00:05:37.367
-Oh, oh.
-Wow.

00:05:37.367 --> 00:05:40.133
-Oh.
-Ooh, that's -- that's electric.

00:05:40.133 --> 00:05:41.434
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.434 --> 00:05:44.067
That's a -- that's --
that's more of a daytime.

00:05:44.067 --> 00:05:46.501
-Yeah.
-"I got stuff to do. Let's go."

00:05:46.501 --> 00:05:48.300
-Now you have
the perfect mix here.

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:50.234
-Gosh, it does.
These both smell great.

00:05:50.234 --> 00:05:52.601
Have you ever tried them
both on?

00:05:52.601 --> 00:05:54.701
-I try to stick to one.
-Okay.

00:05:54.701 --> 00:05:56.601
-Yeah.
-Shower, and then I go

00:05:56.601 --> 00:05:57.601
for the next one.

00:05:57.601 --> 00:05:59.200
-I love it, bud.
This is great.

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:03.634
And it is -- it's Next Chapter.
Volume One, Volume Two.

00:06:03.634 --> 00:06:05.467
How are you liking
being an analyst, by the way?

00:06:05.467 --> 00:06:06.701
You do a great job.

00:06:06.701 --> 00:06:09.901
-I love it. You know,
it's a great way for me

00:06:09.901 --> 00:06:11.334
to stay connected to the game.

00:06:11.334 --> 00:06:15.300
Hockey's been my life since
I was probably 5, 6 years old.

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:18.033
I'm done playing, but now I get
an opportunity to talk about it.

00:06:18.033 --> 00:06:21.334
I mean, amazing people,
TNT out in Atlanta,

00:06:21.334 --> 00:06:23.067
but also working at MSG Network

00:06:23.067 --> 00:06:24.801
here in New York,
covering the Rangers.

00:06:24.801 --> 00:06:28.167
And, to me, it's about
the people, you know?

00:06:28.167 --> 00:06:29.567
Is it fun to talk about hockey?

00:06:29.567 --> 00:06:32.067
Yeah, it's fun,
but the best part is the people

00:06:32.067 --> 00:06:34.901
and the teamwork
and just having fun together.

00:06:34.901 --> 00:06:36.501
That's what matters
to me the most.

00:06:36.501 --> 00:06:39.601
-You're crushing it right now,
buddy, and I'm so happy for you.

00:06:39.601 --> 00:06:40.901
Congratulations on
the Hall of Fame.

00:06:40.901 --> 00:06:42.367
-Thank you so much.
-You know, Henrik,

00:06:42.367 --> 00:06:43.868
whenever you want to come by
here, you're more than welcome.

00:06:43.868 --> 00:06:45.434
-I'm so excited about next time.

00:06:45.434 --> 00:06:47.033
-Next time, we're going --
we're going to space, baby.

00:06:47.033 --> 00:06:49.067
-We're going to space.
-Henrik Lundqvist.

00:06:49.067 --> 00:06:52.634
Watch "NHL on TNT"
every Wednesday night.

00:06:52.634 --> 00:06:54.300
Kelly Clarkson performs
after the break.

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:55.801
Stick around, everybody.

